== Architectural Limitation

The architecture's main limits are single points in the data tier (AISS-01, AISS-05, AISS-10), unproven capacity (AISS-12), drills not yet run on AWS (AISS-13) and unproven alarm delivery (AISS-16). Each is the accepted price of a decision in §3.1–§3.3, and @tbl-aiss names that decision. Most are cost choices for a system that runs a few hours a week; the account-level gaps (AISS-17 to AISS-19) and the image-delivery gaps (AISS-20 to AISS-22) are the exception and belong to the first production phase.

*Roadmap.* Each open item is assigned to one phase (@tbl-roadmap). R0 is closed: the sessions of 9–11 November supplied the placement evidence (AISS-07), two rebuilds from zero and the load reruns (§4.1). The drills of AISS-13 and the fix of AISS-14 were not run by the status date and move to R1. R1 and R2 apply only if the platform continues after the course; their dates assume a go-live decision in December 2026.

